  "units": [
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13",
      "type": "proposition",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13",
      "physical_page": 121,
      "english_source": "content/en/p121.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 77,
        "end": 85
      },
      "summary": "A functorial distinguished-triangle assignment, together with countable products or countable coproducts, forces every arrow to have a split projection-then-inclusion form.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:formula:triangle-assignment",
      "type": "formula",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-tr-assignment",
      "physical_page": 121,
      "english_source": "content/en/p121.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 86,
        "end": 91
      },
      "summary": "For an arrow f from X to Y, denote the functorially selected triangle by X to Y to T(f) to X shifted by one.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:hypothesis:countable-products-or-coproducts",
      "type": "hypothesis",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-countability-hypothesis",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 9,
        "end": 12
      },
      "summary": "Assume that either all countable products or all countable coproducts needed in the triangulated category exist.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:proof:annihilated-morphism",
      "type": "proof_step",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-proof-morphism",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 13,
        "end": 16
      },
      "summary": "Fix an arrow v into the source of f whose composite with f is zero, and regard it as a morphism from the arrow W to zero into f.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:diagram:arrow-square",
      "type": "diagram",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-morphism-square",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 17,
        "end": 25
      },
      "summary": "The relation f composed with v equals zero gives the commuting square between the arrows W to zero and X to Y.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:diagram:triangle-morphism",
      "type": "diagram",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-1",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 26,
        "end": 45
      },
      "summary": "Functoriality sends the arrow square to a morphism from the selected triangle of W to zero into the selected triangle of f.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:claim:zero-target-boundary-isomorphism",
      "type": "claim",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-bottom-triangle",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 46,
        "end": 50
      },
      "summary": "In the selected distinguished triangle of the zero-target arrow W to zero, the boundary from its third object to the shift of W is invertible.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:construction:alpha",
      "type": "construction",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-alpha-definition",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 51,
        "end": 57
      },
      "summary": "Shift the third component of the triangle morphism and compose it with the shifted inverse boundary to define a map alpha(v) from W to T(f) shifted by minus one.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:diagram:alpha-lift",
      "type": "diagram",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-alpha-diagram",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 58,
        "end": 69
      },
      "summary": "The constructed alpha(v) lifts v through the shifted boundary of the selected triangle and its composite with f is zero.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:claim:kernel-section",
      "type": "claim",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-alpha-section",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 70,
        "end": 77
      },
      "summary": "Naturality in annihilated arrows makes alpha a section of the canonical transformation from the functor represented by T(f) shifted by minus one onto the kernel functor of f.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "proposed_new_lemma",
        "label": "lemma-functorial-triangles-decomposable",
        "disposition": "authored_candidate_payload"
      },
      "status": "mapped_payload_authored_built_validated"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:claim:projector-kernel",
      "type": "claim",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-projector-kernel",
      "physical_page": 122,
      "english_source": "content/en/p122.tex",
      "english_lines": {
        "start": 78,
        "end": 81
      },
      "summary": "The kernel functor is a retract of a representable functor and hence is controlled by an idempotent on T(f) shifted by minus one; countable products or coproducts split that idempotent.",
      "target": {
        "kind": "existing_stacks_result",
        "tag": "05QW",
        "label": "derived-lemma-projectors-have-images-triangulated",
        "disposition": "duplicate_excluded_from_new_payload"
      },
      "status": "dispositioned_existing_no_payload"
    },
    {
      "id": "verdier:ast239:1.2.13:conclusion:decomposable",
      "type": "conclusion",
      "anchor_id": "ch2-1-2-13-proof-complete",
